ified the full list of engine gaps and which cards share each seam. No PLAN.md has been written yet. No engine or card files have been modified (correctly, since this is planning-only).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `/workspace/PLAN.md` — the sole deliverable — with the three required sections (Engine gaps table; Per-card plan with nearest FDN analogue and exact seams; Implementation order grouped by shared seam). This is directly in line with the user's explicit request: \"What to produce: `/workspace/PLAN.md`\" and \"`PLAN.md` is your **entire** handoff. Write it for an implementer who has not read what you read.\" Before writing, I may optionally grep RULEBOOK.txt and read a couple more FDN examples (surveil fdn_49/53, counterspell fdn_72/141, SpellCast trigger fdn_245) to confirm details for sos_57, sos_97, sos_201, sos_226 — but writing PLAN.md is the primary next step. (Note: PLAN.md is the ONLY file I am permitted to write this phase — no edits to `engine/` or `cards/sos/*/card_impl.py`.)\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/29d12edd-e81c-4550-a480-8db127b1d09f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"29d12edd-e81c-4550-a480-8db127b1d09f","uuid":"80a7724b-d980-4094-b267-a0ed79baab97","timestamp":"2026-06-04T02:27:01.365Z","isSynthetic":true}
